 "ref": "In October twenty twenty-one, Horwitz pleaded guilty to one count of securities fraud. In his plea agreement, he admitted that he was in fact guilty and agreed to a statement of facts. That statement is the source of much of what you have heard in this story. On February fourteenth, twenty twenty-two, U.S. District Judge Mark C. Scarsi sentenced him to two hundred forty months in federal prison: twenty years. The judge also ordered him to pay two hundred thirty million, three hundred sixty-one thousand, eight hundred eighty-four dollars in restitution. The remaining charges, including wire fraud, were dismissed on the government's motion, as the plea agreement provided.",
